WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.057 --> 00:00:12.260
Morgan was walking her dog, Pip, with her friend Rasha.

2
00:00:13.941 --> 00:00:17.985
Suddenly a big dog raced toward them, barking loudly.

3
00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.148
Pip pulled hard on his leash.

4
00:00:23.729 --> 00:00:28.533
Then, before Morgan could tighten her grip, the leash flew from her hand.

5
00:00:29.754 --> 00:00:35.459
As Pip took off toward the playground, the big dog ran after him, growling and barking.

6
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.464
The two dogs tore around the slide, through the sandbox, and around the swings.

7
00:00:47.469 --> 00:00:50.072
Then Pip darted toward the tennis court.

8
00:00:54.055 --> 00:00:54.355
got him!"

9
00:00:54.716 --> 00:00:57.498
a tennis player called, grabbing Pip's leash.

10
00:00:59.884 --> 00:01:02.506
"Whew!" Morgan ran over and scooped up her dog.

11
00:01:02.526 --> 00:01:04.708
"Thank you!"

12
00:01:04.728 --> 00:01:09.671
A young guy with a skateboard appeared and whistled at the big dog.

13
00:01:09.691 --> 00:01:12.093
"Dakota! Come!"

14
00:01:12.113 --> 00:01:15.615
"Hey!" Morgan called.

15
00:01:15.635 --> 00:01:19.939
"Your dog chased my dog all over the park!"

16
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:22.440
"Relax, kid.

17
00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:23.341
It's totally fine."

18
00:01:25.102 --> 00:01:25.863
"No, it's not!"

19
00:01:26.163 --> 00:01:26.924
Rasha said.

20
00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:31.830
"Pip could have gotten bitten, or he could have run out into the street!

21
00:01:33.031 --> 00:01:34.792
You should keep your dog on a leash!"

22
00:01:35.952 --> 00:01:39.094
Dakota ran off again, chasing a squirrel this time.

23
00:01:44.617 --> 00:01:45.978
The skateboarder shrugged.

24
00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:49.900
Then he dropped his board and skated away.

25
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.102
Morgan could still feel her heart thumping in her chest.

26
00:01:54.122 --> 00:01:57.024
"That was terrifying."

27
00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:00.369
"We need to do something!"

28
00:02:00.809 --> 00:02:01.750
Rasha fumed.

29
00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:05.032
"Our city doesn't have a leash law.

30
00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.313
Let's tell the city council to enact one.

31
00:02:09.874 --> 00:02:12.616
It's not safe for dogs to run loose in the park."

32
00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.781
there's just one problem," Morgan said.

33
00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:25.103
"We're kids.

34
00:02:25.683 --> 00:02:27.004
Who's going to listen to us?"

35
00:02:29.128 --> 00:02:32.210
"In a democracy we have rights too," Rasha said.

36
00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:35.793
"Besides, my mom used to work at City Hall.

37
00:02:36.193 --> 00:02:37.354
So I have some ideas!"

38
00:02:39.515 --> 00:02:41.317
Morgan and Rasha got busy.

39
00:02:42.698 --> 00:02:48.162
First, they sent a letter to the newspaper about why their city needed a leash law to keep

40
00:02:48.262 --> 00:02:49.042
dogs safe.

41
00:02:51.224 --> 00:02:56.948
Next, they sent emails to friends and neighbors, asking them to call local politicians.

42
00:02:58.852 --> 00:03:01.034
After that, they created a petition.

43
00:03:01.054 --> 00:03:07.480
"We need to collect lots of signatures," Rasha said.

44
00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:12.765
"That will show the city council that lots of citizens want a leash law."

45
00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:20.091
Morgan and Rasha brought the petition to locations all over the city.

46
00:03:22.894 --> 00:03:25.396
Some people said they didn't want to sign it.

47
00:03:27.256 --> 00:03:29.919
"My dog likes to run without a leash."

48
00:03:29.939 --> 00:03:34.162
"We already have too many rules!"

49
00:03:35.844 --> 00:03:37.645
But others were eager to sign.

50
00:03:38.927 --> 00:03:43.331
One man even nodded after Morgan told him about how Dakota had chased Pip.

51
00:03:44.632 --> 00:03:47.374
"I've seen Dakota running wild through the park," he said.

52
00:03:47.394 --> 00:03:49.796
"Where do I sign?"

53
00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:57.818
The following week Rasha's mom drove the girls to City Hall for a city council meeting.

54
00:03:58.919 --> 00:04:00.960
The girls waited for their turn to speak.

55
00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:05.243
"You have five minutes," the president said.

56
00:04:06.784 --> 00:04:11.726
Rasha explained why the city needed a leash law to protect dogs and dog owners.

57
00:04:12.967 --> 00:04:15.048
Then Morgan held up their petition.

58
00:04:15.068 --> 00:04:18.310
"We collected hundreds of signatures.

59
00:04:19.331 --> 00:04:21.032
Lots of people want a leash law."

60
00:04:22.892 --> 00:04:24.093
The president nodded.

61
00:04:24.113 --> 00:04:27.455
"We've gotten dozens of calls."

62
00:04:29.115 --> 00:04:30.776
Another council member frowned.

63
00:04:30.796 --> 00:04:34.919
"I have more important things to do," he muttered.

64
00:04:34.939 --> 00:04:38.761
"Protecting kids' dogs is a waste of my time."

65
00:04:42.423 --> 00:04:45.884
you for bringing this issue to our attention, girls," the president said.

66
00:04:45.904 --> 00:04:48.386
"We'll vote on it at our next meeting."

67
00:04:50.107 --> 00:04:52.108
Morgan sighed as she sat down.

68
00:04:53.745 --> 00:04:54.385
"What now?"

69
00:04:54.405 --> 00:04:57.427
"We wait," Rasha said.

70
00:04:57.448 --> 00:05:00.730
"Change never happens overnight."

71
00:05:02.591 --> 00:05:05.353
A month later the girls were walking Pip in the park.

72
00:05:05.373 --> 00:05:10.637
"Look!" Rasha pointed to a workman posting a sign.

73
00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:17.021
dogs must be on a leash.

74
00:05:18.302 --> 00:05:20.244
Violators will be fined."

75
00:05:21.853 --> 00:05:23.098
She hugged Morgan.

76
00:05:23.118 --> 00:05:26.029
"We did it!"

77
00:05:26.471 --> 00:05:27.415
Morgan cheered.
